    "column_stride": "0x0100",
    "mechanism": "Init_Enemy reads the base word, then overwrites its low byte with the record's byte 4; X = (base & 0xFF00) | byte4. Load_Enemy_Into_RAM / EnemySpawn_Scene do 'add.b d2,($FFFFFB12).w' with d2 = 1 between the three Init_Enemy calls. On the 68000 the byte at the word address is the high byte, so the base advances by 0x100 per column and keeps advancing across blocks.",
